<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">ttttt  nNotes:ttttt  n1) The above financial results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee at their meeting held on 21st May, 2019 and thereafter approved by the Board of Directors at their meeting held on 21st May, 2019.t  n2) The financial results for the year ended 31st March, 2019 have been audited by the statutory auditors of the Company. The statutory auditors have expressed an unmodified opinion.tttt  n3) This statement has been prepared in accordance with the Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules, 2015 (Ind AS) prescribed under Section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 and other recognised accounting practices and policies to the extent applicable. tt  n4) On 1st April, 2018, the Company adopted Ind AS 115  Revenue from Contracts with Customers  using the cumulative catch-up transition method applied to contracts that were not completed as of 1st April, 2018. Accordingly, the comparative have not been retrospectively adjusted. The adoption of Ind AS 115 did not have any material impact on the standalone financial results for the quarter and year ended 31st March, 2019.t   n5) Post applicability of Goods and Service Tax (GST) with effect from 1st July, 2017, Total Income from Operations are disclosed net of GST while revenue for the period up to 30th June, 2017 is including excise duty. Accordingly, Total Income from Operations for the year ended on 31st March, 2019 are not comparable with the corresponding figures of the previous period.tt  n6) The Board of Directors of the Company has recommended the final dividend of Rs. 1.20/- per share (nominal value of Rs.2/- each). The final dividend, if declared at the ensuing Annual General Meeting will result in cash outflow of Rs. 114.18 Millions (including dividend distribution tax).t  n7) The Share Allotment Committee of the Board at its meeting held on 25th September, 2018 allotted 5,64,000 Equity Shares to eligibile employees of the Company pursuant to  KEI Employee Stock Option Scheme-2015  (3rd Year). Further, Nomination and Remuneration Committee of the Board at its meeting held on25th September, 2018 has granted 15,000 Stock Option to eligible employee pursuant to KEI Employee Stock Option Scheme-2015 which will vest in one (1)  year from the date of grant.tttt  n8) During the year, Company has incorporated a Company in South Africa with 49% shareholding of the Company, under the name  KEI Cables SA (Pty) Limited.ttttt  n9) The figures of the last quarter are the balancing figures in respect of standalone financial results between audited figures of the financial year ended 31st March, 2019 and the published year to date figures upto third quarter i.e. 31st December, 2018 of the current year. Also the figures upto the end of the third quarter   nhad only been reviewed and not subjected to audit.tttt  n10) Previous year / periods figures have been regrouped / reclassified, wherever necessary. tt  n11) The above results of the Company are available on the Company's website www.kei-ind.com and also at www.bseindia.com and www.nseindia.com.  n </in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
